Package: pulsaros-librepods
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Victor Rosario <hello@victorrosario.dev>
Depends: bluez, libqt6bluetooth6, libqt6core6t64, libqt6dbus6, libqt6gui6, libqt6network6, libqt6qml6, libqt6quick6, libqt6quickcontrols2-6, libqt6widgets6, libpulse0, libssl3t64, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtquick-window
Recommends: pipewire-pulse
Description: AirPods daemon for Pulsar OS (battery, listening modes, ear detection)
 A headless daemon that talks to AirPods over Bluetooth (Apple Accessory Protocol
 and BLE advertisements) and publishes their state as a JSON file, with a small
 command line (librepods-ctl) to change the listening mode, Conversation
 Awareness, One-Bud ANC and ear detection. The GNOME Shell extension in
 pulsaros-airpods draws the top-bar icon and popover from it.
 .
 This is a modified copy of the omarchy-pods daemon, itself a fork of librepods
 by Kavish Devar. Licensed GPL-3.0; see /usr/share/doc/pulsaros-librepods.
